list.item:
 Castelo Branco, Humberto de Alencar, General;
Chief of Staff of the Army in Brazil until April 1964; President of Brazil
from April 15, 1964, until March 15, 1967

 Montagne Sánchez, Ernesto, Major General;
Peruvian Prime Minister and Minister of War from January 1969 until 1972;
President of Cabinet-Council and Minister of War from 1971

 Walters, Vernon A., Lieutenant General, USA;
Senior Department of Defense Attaché in France from 1969 until May 1972;
Deputy Director of Central Intelligence from May 1972

person.note:
Director of the Western Hemisphere Department of the World Bank until 1969;
                    Director, South American Department, from 1970 until 1971; Regional Vice
                    President of the Latin American Region from 1972

Political Officer, U.S. Embassy in Rio de Janeiro, until September 1970;
                    Bureau of Inter-American Affairs, Department of State, from September
                    1970

Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Inter-American Affairs from April 1969
                    until March 5, 1970; Acting Assistant Secretary from March until June 11, 1973;
                    thereafter, U.S. Ambassador to Brazil

Counselor for Political Affairs, U.S. Embassy in Brasilia, from January 1969;
                    Director, Brazilian Office, Bureau of Inter-American Affairs, Department of
                    State, from December 1971

Assistant Deputy Director for Coordination, Bureau of Intelligence and
                    Research, Department of State, from January 20, 1969, until January 1, 1972;
                    Deputy Director from Jan 1, 1972

Office of Research and Analysis for American Republics, Bureau of Intelligence
                    and Research, Department of State, from January 1969 until September 1970;
                    Political Officer, U.S. Embassy in Guatemala City, from September 1970
